WEBVTT

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.402
All right, all right, hold on.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.273
If you were married in 2304,

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.108
and your daughter was conceived
during your 11th Pon farr,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.616
that would make you...
162 years old.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.616
Incorrect.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.414
Come on, Tom.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.114
The man's not a day over 140.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.621
We know you were
at least a hundred

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.624
when you joined Starfleet
the second time,

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:29.128
so I'm guessing
you're around 133?

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.457
Also incorrect.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.794
I'm afraid you both lack
sufficient data

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.164
to reach a logical conclusion.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.964
Come on, Tuvok, tell us.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.902
I see no reason
to enlighten you.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.064
Don't tell me Vulcans

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.971
are embarrassed about their age.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.636
On the contrary,
we value the wisdom

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.576
that comes with advancing years.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.479
In that case, how wise are you?

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.983
Wise enough to end this inquiry.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.285
Saved by the bell.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:58.324
I've got a fleet of ships
200,000 kilometers dead ahead.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:00:59.688
Can you identify them?

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:00.817
Negative.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.919
I'm reading multiple
hull configurations.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:03.927
Raise shields.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.930
Red Alert.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.591
Report.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.931
We've detected a large group
of vessels directly ahead.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.265
- Hostile?
- Possibly.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.429
I'm charging weapons.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.336
On screen.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.274
I'm counting 62 ships

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.108
and a few hundred
pieces of ships

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.773
all dead in space.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:23.941
It's a junkyard.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.450
Congratulations, Tuvok.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.610
You just saved us

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.950
from a flotilla
of hostile trash.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:30.955
We're being hailed.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.321
Let's see what they want.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:36.726
Welcome to Abaddon's Repository
of Lost Treasures.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.458
Whether you're in the mood
to buy or simply browse,

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.692
we're always open.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.962
Take a look.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:46.403
You may find something
you never knew you wanted.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.957
Mr. Abaddon.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.788
The name was passed down
from my father

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.122
and his father before him.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.628
Not a very imaginative lot,

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.460
but I'll answer to it
just the same.

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.625
I'm Commander Chakotay.
This is Mr. Neelix.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.633
Welcome to Voyager.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:56.634
Neelix, is it?

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.796
You wouldn't be
a fellow trader, would you?

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.304
What makes you say that?

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.068
Cheerful demeanor, furtive eyes.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.904
It's obvious
you're a man of commerce.

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:05.911
You're very perceptive,
Mr. Abaddon.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.742
A useful skill
in my line of work.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:10.578
Oh, I'll admit there was a time
when I dabbled in commerce,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.413
but these days,
I focus my efforts

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.077
on food and diplomacy.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.917
Well, whether you're interested
in a new iso-convective oven

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.083
or a slightly dated
translation matrix,

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.591
you've come to the right place.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.753
My inventory,
give or take a few items.

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:25.593
After 20 years,
it's hard to keep up.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.098
Looks like you have
an item or two

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.428
we might be interested in.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.763
Uh, the question is

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.600
what are you looking
for in return?

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.264
Artificial gravity plating.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.104
Plasma-based power induction.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.108
Impressive.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.610
Those are integrated systems.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.613
Unfortunately, we couldn't
trade them to you

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:43.546
without dismantling
our whole ship.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.709
Commander, don't
we have some spare

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.776
duranium sheeting
in Cargo Bay 1?

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.788
With a few modifications, uh,

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.619
it could be converted
into gravity plating.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:55.457
Good idea. Why don't you show
Mr. Abaddon our inventory?

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.790
Report back when you're done.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:59.991
Yes, sir. Mr. Abaddon,
follow me, please.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:04.560
This guy's collected more
technology than the Borg.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.231
And almost all of it
is useless.

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.571
Wait. What's that?

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.904
Ensign?

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.104
Grid 49-Alpha.

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:18.917
Oh, she's beautiful.

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.247
It's just an old rust bucket.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.151
What, are you kidding?
Look at those lines.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.917
It's a work of art.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:28.255
That ship wasn't assembled;
it was sculpted.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:30.455
I think I'm in love.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.601
That makes 15 power regulators
in fair condition

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.762
and three more we could salvage
with a little work.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.773
Seven has some doubts
about the ion exchange rods...

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:42.933
We'll take a chance.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.270
Add them to the list.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.437
What about these
cultural artifacts?

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.638
Oh, just a few items

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:50.444
I thought might have
some historical value.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.778
They don't cost much.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:54.115
Looks like a good haul.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:55.211
If that's it...

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:58.280
Oh, uh, yes, there is
one other item:

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:02.192
Uh, a small vessel
that could be an asset.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.058
We've already got
a full complement of shuttles,

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.722
not to mention the Delta Flyer.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:08.130
What do we need
with this derelict ship?

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:11.227
Chakotay, this ship
is a diamond in the rough.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.568
Sure, it's got
some scrapes and scratches,

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.904
but, here, take a look
at these systems.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:22.073
It has a neurogenic interface
that allows it to react

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.911
directly
to the pilot's thoughts.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.075
That gives it the potential
of being quicker

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:27.779
and more maneuverable
than anything we've got,

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:29.253
including the Delta Flyer.

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.517
Add to that
an optronic weapons array...

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.582
I get the picture.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.889
Are you sure you're not just
looking for a new toy?

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.260
No. Absolutely not.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:40.424
Even B'Elanna thinks
restoring this ship

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.434
is worthwhile.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:44.231
Maybe, if we had the manpower
to restore it.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.931
No, I'll do all the work
myself on my own time...

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:50.601
and if I need a hand,
Harry's offered to help.

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.940
I have?

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:55.912
What will it cost us?

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.109
Abaddon's agreed to give it
to us for three used power cells

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:00.277
and Tom's interactive
record collection.

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:01.786
My jukebox.

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:05.557
All right.

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:09.721
One slightly used alien ship.

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.525
Don't make me regret this.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:13.189
You won't.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.059
Remember, just one seat.
Not much storage.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.569
She was designed for
speed, not hauling.

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:19.570
Understood.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:20.901
Make sure you go easy
on the thrusters.

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.235
She doesn't like
being manhandled.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:23.570
- Temperamental?
- Sensitive.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:24.575
She demands respect,

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.236
like any fine piece
of machinery.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:27.904
Sounds like you're sorry
to let her go.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.413
Well, in some ways,
she's like the daughter

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:31.074
that I couldn't marry off,
but that doesn't mean

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.583
I'd trade her to just anyone.

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:35.246
I've got a feeling you're the
kind of pilot that she needs,

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:37.915
someone that'll give her the
proper care and attention.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.082
I'm your man.

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.250
Don't worry, Mr. Abaddon.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:41.759
She's in good hands.

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:44.922
Well, this has been
a very productive exchange.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.760
Oh, just one more thing...

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:47.925
Uh, let me guess.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.900
All trades are final.

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:02.707
I still can't get
an active readout.

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.511
Here's the reason.

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:06.711
Another damaged power cell.

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:09.016
Come on, Alice, how 'bout it?

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:10.020
Give us a break.

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:12.250
Alice?

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.452
Well, I've got
to call her something.

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:17.462
How about the Lost Cause?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.897
Alice Battisti was
"the lost cause."

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.559
I knew her back at the Academy.

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:25.069
She was smart, sexy...

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:27.435
but she wouldn't give me
the time of day.

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.908
All right, Alice it is.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:32.376
Try it again.

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:37.878
I've got a pulse!

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:41.915
A little snug.

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:45.082
As Seven would say,
an efficient design.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.921
The main computer's
coming on line.

00:08:47.994 --> 00:08:49.894
There's not much in it.

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:50.929
Just a few schematics.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.260
Looks like somebody tried
to wipe the database.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.926
Probably rolled
the odometer back, too.

00:08:56.002 --> 00:09:00.166
Let's see what this
neurogenic interface can do.

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:05.540
Whoa.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:08.375
What's it like?

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:10.711
It's kind of hard to describe.

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:13.047
I'm tapped into all
the primary systems:

00:09:13.119 --> 00:09:16.486
Ops, tactical, sensors...

00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:19.553
What happened?

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:21.718
We just blew out
two more power cells.

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:26.898
See if you can reconfigure
the power distribution grid.

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.125
Look, we're both tired.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.896
Why don't we call it a night,
come back fresh tomorrow?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.734
Oh, come on, we can still get
a couple more hours in.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.398
You can get
a couple more hours in.

00:09:35.474 --> 00:09:37.271
I'm going to bed.

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:42.774
All right. You win.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:53.257
Good night, Alice.

00:09:53.326 --> 00:09:56.124
See you in the morning.

00:10:16.349 --> 00:10:17.941
Good night, Alice.

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:20.281
See you in the morning.

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:22.821
See you in the morning.

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:27.621
See you in the morning.
See you in the morning.

00:10:27.693 --> 00:10:30.787
See you in the morning.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.168
Tom...

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:42.007
B'Elanna?

00:11:04.497 --> 00:11:06.795
Tom?

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:19.443
Who are you?

00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:23.642
It's me, Alice.

00:11:35.695 --> 00:11:38.664
Good morning, Alice.

00:12:28.013 --> 00:12:32.109
I'm sorry, but you're going
to have to trust me on this.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:35.950
You'll be a lot happier
if we can bypass the EPS relays.

00:12:36.021 --> 00:12:37.784
- Tom.
- Yeah?

00:12:37.857 --> 00:12:39.449
Who are you talking to?

00:12:39.525 --> 00:12:42.961
Alice. She's being
very stubborn today.

00:12:43.028 --> 00:12:44.962
No matter what I do,
I can't get her

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.294
to bring her propulsion
systems on line.

00:12:47.366 --> 00:12:49.300
Next question:
What are you wearing?

00:12:49.368 --> 00:12:54.305
Oh, this is a flight suit design
I found in Alice's database,

00:12:54.373 --> 00:12:56.967
something her last
pilot used to wear.

00:12:57.042 --> 00:12:59.135
For a minute, I thought

00:12:59.211 --> 00:13:02.237
you were changing
Captain Proton's look.

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:03.906
Chapter 37?

00:13:03.983 --> 00:13:05.416
Oh, "The Web of Pain."

00:13:05.484 --> 00:13:06.746
I completely forgot.

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:10.778
Oh, no problem... I've got
another hour on the holodeck.

00:13:11.824 --> 00:13:15.089
You know, now is
not a great time.

00:13:15.161 --> 00:13:16.753
How 'bout tomorrow?

00:13:16.829 --> 00:13:18.421
That's what you said yesterday.

00:13:18.497 --> 00:13:20.590
Sorry, Harry.
Alice needs me.

00:13:20.666 --> 00:13:21.758
So does Arachnia.

00:13:21.834 --> 00:13:24.598
Give the queen my regards.

00:13:27.506 --> 00:13:29.974
Okay...

00:13:35.347 --> 00:13:37.281
Seven, can I get you something?

00:13:37.349 --> 00:13:38.475
A refund.

00:13:38.551 --> 00:13:41.179
The star charts we obtained
from Abaddon are inaccurate.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:42.413
Really?

00:13:42.488 --> 00:13:45.116
The computations are
based on obsolete data.

00:13:45.191 --> 00:13:47.455
It's not the only item
that didn't live up

00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:49.619
to its advertising.

00:13:49.695 --> 00:13:51.629
Cultural artifacts?

00:13:51.697 --> 00:13:53.130
According to Abaddon,

00:13:53.199 --> 00:13:55.463
they're lost treasures
of the Delta Quadrant.

00:13:55.534 --> 00:13:58.128
If you ask me,
they're worthless trinkets.

00:13:58.204 --> 00:14:00.638
Perhaps not.

00:14:00.706 --> 00:14:02.731
This crystal is beryllium.

00:14:02.808 --> 00:14:04.366
Valuable?

00:14:04.443 --> 00:14:06.411
Beryllium is the
standard currency

00:14:06.478 --> 00:14:08.241
in Spatial Grid 539.

00:14:08.314 --> 00:14:09.747
There are species
that would trade

00:14:09.815 --> 00:14:12.750
an entire fleet of starships
for this "trinket."

00:14:12.818 --> 00:14:14.752
If Abaddon knew about this,

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:17.584
he'd never have traded it
for a few plasma couplings.

00:14:17.656 --> 00:14:20.090
Well, maybe I should return it.

00:14:20.159 --> 00:14:24.289
Need I remind you?
All trades are final.

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:28.425
Neelix, I need one
bottle of champagne,

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.432
if you don't mind.

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:30.593
Another anniversary?

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:32.899
No. I'm christening Alice.

00:14:32.972 --> 00:14:34.599
Congratulations.

00:14:34.673 --> 00:14:36.937
I'll whip up some hors d'oeuvres
for the crew.

00:14:37.009 --> 00:14:38.772
Oh, no, don't bother.

00:14:38.844 --> 00:14:42.439
This is a private ceremony.
Just me and B'Elanna.

00:14:42.514 --> 00:14:43.776
And Alice, of course.

00:14:43.849 --> 00:14:45.111
Oh, yes, of course.

00:14:45.184 --> 00:14:47.618
There's nothing like having
your own ship.

00:14:47.686 --> 00:14:49.620
I remember
when I first laid eyes

00:14:49.688 --> 00:14:51.747
on my little freighter, Baxial.

00:14:51.824 --> 00:14:53.951
No, don't tell me...
love at first sight?

00:14:54.026 --> 00:14:56.620
Actually, I thought she was
the ugliest thing I ever saw.

00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:59.459
But she grew on me.

00:14:59.531 --> 00:15:02.398
Eventually, I-I couldn't
imagine being without her.

00:15:02.468 --> 00:15:04.493
You know, she's still down
in the Shuttle Bay.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:05.901
Why don't we get her
and Alice together

00:15:05.971 --> 00:15:06.903
and go on a double date?

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:08.405
You pack the picnic basket.

00:15:08.474 --> 00:15:09.941
I'll bring the deuterium.

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:14.235
So, I finally get
to meet the other woman.

00:15:14.313 --> 00:15:15.245
Well, don't be too critical.

00:15:15.314 --> 00:15:16.747
She's a long way from finished.

00:15:16.815 --> 00:15:18.248
When have you ever known me
to be critical?

00:15:18.317 --> 00:15:20.911
Is that a trick question?

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:23.955
Okay, ready?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.695
Well?

00:15:36.769 --> 00:15:38.100
It's beautiful.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.138
I can hardly believe
it's the same ship.

00:15:40.205 --> 00:15:42.105
Yeah. Most of it isn't.

00:15:42.174 --> 00:15:44.438
I've replaced
the impulse reactor,

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:47.604
navigational array,
uh, plasma manifolds...

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.944
The list goes on and on.

00:15:50.015 --> 00:15:53.109
Just a few more repairs,
and she'll be spaceworthy.

00:15:53.185 --> 00:15:55.779
Care to do the honors?

00:15:55.854 --> 00:15:59.950
It's almost a shame
to break this over the hull.

00:16:00.025 --> 00:16:01.694
You have a point.

00:16:03.963 --> 00:16:07.228
Oh, oh, be careful...
the upholstery.

00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:09.893
I'll send an Engineering team
down to clean it up.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.939
- To Alice.
- To Alice.

00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:18.238
So, when's her first flight?

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.743
Well, a couple of days,

00:16:19.812 --> 00:16:22.406
if I can round up
all the parts I need.

00:16:22.481 --> 00:16:24.574
You want to come with me?

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.413
Sure there's room?

00:16:26.485 --> 00:16:28.077
Lt'll be a tight squeeze.

00:16:28.153 --> 00:16:30.587
We'll manage.

00:16:32.191 --> 00:16:33.590
Hold on.

00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:35.251
Something wrong?

00:16:35.327 --> 00:16:38.922
It's these
environmental controls.

00:16:38.998 --> 00:16:40.260
They need recalibrating.

00:16:40.332 --> 00:16:41.924
It is kind of warm
in here, isn't it?

00:16:42.001 --> 00:16:44.595
Alice, lower
the ambient temperature.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.604
Please specify, Tom.

00:16:46.672 --> 00:16:48.606
Five degrees should do it.

00:16:48.674 --> 00:16:50.938
Temperature modification
complete.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:52.944
That's some voice.

00:16:53.012 --> 00:16:56.277
It came with the ship.

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:57.940
You jealous?

00:16:58.017 --> 00:17:00.281
Maybe I should be.

00:17:00.352 --> 00:17:02.377
I hear you've been
sleeping here.

00:17:02.454 --> 00:17:04.388
When Alice lets me sleep.

00:17:04.456 --> 00:17:07.254
Sounds like a real slave driver.

00:17:11.964 --> 00:17:14.558
Well, if you're trying
to make improvements,

00:17:14.633 --> 00:17:15.565
you might want to start

00:17:15.634 --> 00:17:16.726
with these
reactant injectors.

00:17:16.802 --> 00:17:18.394
The deuterium mix is too high.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:21.598
Well, that's
how Alice likes it.

00:17:23.642 --> 00:17:25.234
No, don't touch that.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:26.902
I was just trying to help.

00:17:26.979 --> 00:17:29.573
Well, thanks, but we're fine.

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:33.584
"We"? It's a ship, Tom.

00:17:33.652 --> 00:17:35.916
Yeah, but she's my ship.

00:17:35.988 --> 00:17:38.582
Well, then, maybe I'll leave
the two of you alone.

00:17:38.657 --> 00:17:40.249
Okay.

00:17:40.325 --> 00:17:42.088
I'll see you later.

00:17:42.161 --> 00:17:44.254
Thanks for the champagne.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.265
Oh, sorry.

00:17:49.334 --> 00:17:52.633
I need to fix that.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:05.710
30 meters of EPS conduit,

00:18:05.784 --> 00:18:07.376
a broadband sensor matrix,

00:18:07.453 --> 00:18:09.045
a tactical data module.

00:18:09.121 --> 00:18:11.055
Tom, I appreciate
your enthusiasm,

00:18:11.123 --> 00:18:12.556
but I can't spare
these parts right now.

00:18:12.624 --> 00:18:14.524
But they're just lying
around Cargo Bay 2.

00:18:14.593 --> 00:18:17.528
Those are emergency supplies,
and this isn't an emergency.

00:18:17.596 --> 00:18:21.225
Okay, what if I just
replicated some?

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:22.733
That takes energy,

00:18:22.801 --> 00:18:25.565
which isn't exactly in
abundance at the moment.

00:18:25.637 --> 00:18:27.229
Maybe in a few weeks,

00:18:27.306 --> 00:18:29.069
if we can replenish
our power reserve.

00:18:29.141 --> 00:18:31.575
A few weeks?

00:18:31.643 --> 00:18:33.736
What am I supposed to do
until then?

00:18:34.813 --> 00:18:37.907
Your duties,
which you've been neglecting.

00:18:37.983 --> 00:18:40.508
You've been late
for two shifts in Sick Bay.

00:18:40.586 --> 00:18:42.383
You've been distracted
on the Bridge.

00:18:42.454 --> 00:18:44.684
Maybe it's time you
gave this project a rest.

00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:49.283
You're right.

00:18:49.361 --> 00:18:51.295
I guess I have been
overdoing it.

00:18:51.363 --> 00:18:53.263
You look run-down.

00:18:53.332 --> 00:18:55.766
Maybe you should
stop by Sick Bay

00:18:55.834 --> 00:18:57.096
and have the Doctor
take a look at you.

00:18:57.169 --> 00:18:58.227
No. I'm fine.

00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:00.635
I-I just haven't been
getting enough sleep.

00:19:00.706 --> 00:19:02.867
Well, your next shift
isn't till 0700.

00:19:02.941 --> 00:19:05.774
Why don't you do yourself
a favor and turn in early?

00:19:06.845 --> 00:19:08.904
Yeah. Good idea.

00:19:10.282 --> 00:19:12.477
One more thing.

00:19:12.551 --> 00:19:13.882
I'd appreciate it if you'd shave

00:19:13.952 --> 00:19:15.886
and change back
into your uniform.

00:19:15.954 --> 00:19:18.115
We do have protocols.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.851
Yes, sir.

00:19:20.893 --> 00:19:23.225
We'll get your Alice flying.

00:19:23.295 --> 00:19:25.263
Just give it some time.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:35.567
Sorry, Alice, we'll have to put
the test flight on hold.

00:19:35.641 --> 00:19:38.075
All we need
is a few lousy spare parts,

00:19:38.143 --> 00:19:40.407
but to listen to Chakotay,
you'd think Voyager

00:19:40.479 --> 00:19:41.912
would grind to a halt
without them.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.242
But we're so close.

00:19:43.315 --> 00:19:45.579
Well, he gave me a direct order.

00:19:45.651 --> 00:19:48.245
Since when do you care
so much about orders?

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.413
I'm already an Ensign.

00:19:50.489 --> 00:19:52.081
You want to see me
busted down to Cadet?

00:19:52.157 --> 00:19:53.419
Don't take that off.

00:19:53.492 --> 00:19:55.926
Well, I'm afraid I have
to get back into uniform.

00:19:55.994 --> 00:19:57.427
Protocol.

00:19:57.496 --> 00:19:59.930
Forget about protocol.

00:19:59.998 --> 00:20:04.435
Once my repairs are complete,
we can go somewhere together.

00:20:04.503 --> 00:20:05.765
Leave Voyager?

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:07.600
It's been a long time
since I met a pilot

00:20:07.673 --> 00:20:09.607
I've been compatible with.

00:20:09.675 --> 00:20:12.644
We can go anywhere you want.

00:20:13.679 --> 00:20:15.613
It's very tempting, Alice,

00:20:15.681 --> 00:20:17.774
but I can't just take off.

00:20:17.849 --> 00:20:19.111
What's holding you back?

00:20:19.184 --> 00:20:21.277
My job, for one thing.

00:20:21.353 --> 00:20:23.947
My friends...

00:20:24.022 --> 00:20:25.614
B'Elanna.

00:20:25.691 --> 00:20:28.626
She doesn't understand you
the way I do.

00:20:28.694 --> 00:20:31.993
None of them do.

00:20:33.532 --> 00:20:35.625
Look, maybe we can
make the test flight

00:20:35.701 --> 00:20:37.293
in a few weeks,
and if it goes well,

00:20:37.369 --> 00:20:38.802
I'm sure the Captain
will assign us

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:40.963
on missions together,
but I can't leave Voyager.

00:20:41.039 --> 00:20:43.974
All right.

00:20:44.042 --> 00:20:47.637
I'm sure you know
what's best for us.

00:20:47.713 --> 00:20:50.648
Yeah, I think I do.

00:20:50.716 --> 00:20:54.311
You look a little tired.

00:20:54.386 --> 00:20:57.844
How about some rest?

00:20:57.923 --> 00:21:01.518
Sit back. Relax.

00:21:03.495 --> 00:21:06.464
Let me help you with this.

00:21:09.334 --> 00:21:10.767
What are these?

00:21:10.836 --> 00:21:13.600
Just some modifications
I made to your flight suit.

00:21:13.672 --> 00:21:17.108
They'll help us
work together more closely.

00:21:17.175 --> 00:21:19.609
I'll show you.

00:21:19.678 --> 00:21:22.442
Activate the interface.

00:21:22.514 --> 00:21:24.948
Just for a minute.

00:21:25.017 --> 00:21:27.986
You won't regret it.

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:41.989
What do you say we continue
with those repairs?

00:21:55.881 --> 00:21:57.644
How's it coming?

00:21:57.716 --> 00:22:00.310
This is the last power cell.

00:22:00.385 --> 00:22:02.615
Then we'll just need
the data module

00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:05.282
from Section Beta-12.

00:22:06.325 --> 00:22:08.259
What's wrong?

00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:10.761
Well, these relays
are just tricky.

00:22:10.829 --> 00:22:11.921
That's all.

00:22:11.997 --> 00:22:13.589
You're not being honest with me.

00:22:13.665 --> 00:22:16.964
I thought we agreed to tell
each other everything.

00:22:19.004 --> 00:22:21.097
Well, it's just...

00:22:21.173 --> 00:22:23.607
we're compromising
vital systems.

00:22:23.675 --> 00:22:25.267
Backup systems.

00:22:25.344 --> 00:22:27.608
If there's an emergency,
Voyager's going to need them.

00:22:27.679 --> 00:22:29.271
If your friends had
been more understanding,

00:22:29.348 --> 00:22:31.441
we wouldn't have to be
sneaking around like this.

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:34.952
I've spent the last six years
with these people.

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:36.954
They're like my family.

00:22:37.022 --> 00:22:40.287
Sometimes you have to
leave your family behind.

00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:42.793
They're not like us.

00:22:42.861 --> 00:22:45.955
They're trapped by
rules and regulations.

00:22:46.031 --> 00:22:49.125
Velocity, freedom...

00:22:49.201 --> 00:22:53.638
they'll never understand
these things the way we do.

00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:56.139
Yeah, maybe you're right.

00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:58.802
Of course I am.

00:22:58.877 --> 00:23:01.471
You don't belong here.

00:23:01.546 --> 00:23:04.947
You belong with me.

00:23:06.485 --> 00:23:10.251
You're thinking about
your first flight, aren't you?

00:23:10.322 --> 00:23:12.950
Tell me.

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:18.459
Dad took me up
in an old S-class shuttle.

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:22.595
Two seats, no warp drive,

00:23:22.667 --> 00:23:25.261
manual helm controls.

00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:27.931
I was eight years old

00:23:28.006 --> 00:23:30.099
and I was scared out of my wits.

00:23:30.175 --> 00:23:31.938
You couldn't keep
the ship level.

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.274
No, not at first...

00:23:34.346 --> 00:23:38.783
but then... came
this moment of clarity,

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:41.614
when suddenly,
everything made sense.

00:23:41.686 --> 00:23:43.620
The clouds parted.

00:23:43.688 --> 00:23:46.316
I was flying.

00:23:49.194 --> 00:23:52.129
No matter how many starships
I've piloted since then,

00:23:52.197 --> 00:23:54.961
I'm still chasing that feeling.

00:23:55.033 --> 00:23:57.968
Tomorrow, you'll catch it...

00:23:58.036 --> 00:23:59.628
only this time, there won't be

00:23:59.704 --> 00:24:02.901
any clumsy controls
to get in the way.

00:24:02.974 --> 00:24:05.067
Just you...

00:24:05.143 --> 00:24:07.077
me...

00:24:07.145 --> 00:24:10.012
and the stars.

00:24:15.654 --> 00:24:16.916
Hey.

00:24:17.055 --> 00:24:19.922
I wasn't aware you were
assigned to Astrometrics.

00:24:19.991 --> 00:24:22.585
I was just, uh, passing by.

00:24:22.661 --> 00:24:25.255
I guess curiosity
got the best of me.

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:26.922
Are you planning
an away mission?

00:24:26.998 --> 00:24:29.091
You were charting a course.

00:24:29.167 --> 00:24:30.600
Oh, that.

00:24:30.669 --> 00:24:34.935
Uh, no, I was just taking a peek
at what's ahead of us.

00:24:35.006 --> 00:24:37.201
All yours.

00:24:37.275 --> 00:24:38.936
You've modified your garment.

00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:41.604
Uh, adapted, actually.

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:42.942
I made a few tweaks

00:24:43.014 --> 00:24:45.278
to enhance Alice's
neurogenic interface.

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:49.446
You know, the "merging
of man and machine"?

00:24:49.521 --> 00:24:52.285
Perhaps you should learn
more about this interface

00:24:52.357 --> 00:24:53.619
before you attempt to use it.

00:24:53.692 --> 00:24:56.126
Convince her it's safe.

00:24:56.194 --> 00:24:58.458
I ran diagnostics
of every system

00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:00.122
onboard that ship.

00:25:00.198 --> 00:25:01.961
There's nothing to worry about.

00:25:02.033 --> 00:25:03.728
Perhaps I should examine it.

00:25:03.802 --> 00:25:07.067
Make an excuse and leave.

00:25:07.138 --> 00:25:12.235
It's nice of you to offer,
but it's really not necessary.

00:25:12.310 --> 00:25:14.540
I have to get back to work.

00:25:22.554 --> 00:25:24.579
Power fluctuation's
down to 4.7 percent.

00:25:24.656 --> 00:25:26.920
Looks like Abaddon's regulators
might work out after all.

00:25:26.992 --> 00:25:28.755
Keep at it...
the last thing we need

00:25:28.827 --> 00:25:30.260
is a temperamental power supply.

00:25:30.328 --> 00:25:32.262
Bad day at the office?

00:25:32.330 --> 00:25:36.596
Bad night with Tom Paris.

00:25:36.668 --> 00:25:38.602
You're his best friend, right?

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:39.932
So he tells me.

00:25:40.005 --> 00:25:42.769
So, maybe you can explain why
every time he finds a new hobby,

00:25:42.841 --> 00:25:44.934
I go right out the airlock.

00:25:45.010 --> 00:25:46.272
I wouldn't take it personally.

00:25:46.344 --> 00:25:49.438
The Ferengi call it the
Five Stages of Acquisition:

00:25:49.514 --> 00:25:52.278
Infatuation, Justification,
Appropriation,

00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:55.285
Obsession and Resale.

00:25:55.353 --> 00:25:57.116
Seems like you've only
got one stage left

00:25:57.188 --> 00:25:58.780
before he loses
interest in that ship.

00:25:58.857 --> 00:26:00.119
Then he's all yours again.

00:26:00.191 --> 00:26:02.216
Until the next infatuation.

00:26:03.962 --> 00:26:07.557
We've got a.003 drop
in the warp field output.

00:26:07.632 --> 00:26:09.065
That's within parameters.

00:26:09.134 --> 00:26:11.193
Not on my watch.

00:26:11.269 --> 00:26:14.033
Somebody's removed
four power cells

00:26:14.105 --> 00:26:15.902
from the secondary
warp assembly

00:26:15.974 --> 00:26:18.238
without authorization.

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:20.244
Whoever it was tried
to cover his tracks

00:26:20.312 --> 00:26:22.405
by rerouting power
from adjacent cells.

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:23.412
Should we tell Tuvok?

00:26:23.481 --> 00:26:24.743
Don't bother.

00:26:24.816 --> 00:26:26.807
This is an open-and-shut case.

00:26:31.323 --> 00:26:34.121
Tom Paris!

00:26:44.502 --> 00:26:46.436
Well, Alice...

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:50.634
Iooks like you've been borrowing
my things without permission.

00:27:07.292 --> 00:27:08.759
Hey!

00:27:11.796 --> 00:27:14.060
Computer, open the hatch.

00:27:14.132 --> 00:27:16.100
Unable to comply.

00:27:17.636 --> 00:27:20.935
Warning. Life support failure.

00:27:23.975 --> 00:27:26.603
Torres to the Bridge.

00:27:28.647 --> 00:27:31.275
Torres to Chakotay!

00:27:32.817 --> 00:27:34.182
Anybody!

00:27:49.501 --> 00:27:51.935
B'Elanna, what are
you doing here?

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:54.130
Let me out of here!

00:27:59.310 --> 00:28:01.244
What the hell happened in there?

00:28:01.312 --> 00:28:03.405
Your ship tried to kill me.

00:28:03.481 --> 00:28:04.573
That's ridiculous.

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:07.584
It sealed the... the hatch,
vented the atmosphere.

00:28:07.652 --> 00:28:09.051
You must have
accidentally tripped

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:10.178
the environmental controls.

00:28:10.255 --> 00:28:12.189
Don't you try to tell me
this was an accident.

00:28:12.257 --> 00:28:13.451
What else could it have been?

00:28:13.525 --> 00:28:15.220
How about "pilot error"?

00:28:16.294 --> 00:28:18.455
Are you saying
that this was my fault?

00:28:18.530 --> 00:28:20.896
What's gotten into you?

00:28:20.965 --> 00:28:23.229
You've been stealing
components, Tom.

00:28:23.301 --> 00:28:24.359
Oh...

00:28:24.436 --> 00:28:25.903
I found the power cells.

00:28:26.037 --> 00:28:27.629
A few spare parts?

00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:29.071
You're overreacting.

00:28:29.140 --> 00:28:30.232
Am I?

00:28:30.308 --> 00:28:31.400
Where are you going?

00:28:31.476 --> 00:28:33.068
- To talk to the Captain.
- Wait.

00:28:33.144 --> 00:28:34.236
There's something
wrong with you.

00:28:34.312 --> 00:28:36.075
- Listen to me!
- Are you out of your mind?

00:28:36.147 --> 00:28:37.580
Stay out of this, B'Elanna!

00:28:37.649 --> 00:28:41.107
Or what? You'll sic Alice
on me again?

00:28:42.153 --> 00:28:44.621
Let her go.

00:28:45.657 --> 00:28:47.090
What were you thinking?!

00:28:47.158 --> 00:28:49.092
You could've killed her!

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:50.422
She broke into my database.

00:28:50.495 --> 00:28:53.089
She was going to discover
our flight plan.

00:28:53.164 --> 00:28:54.756
Not that it matters now.

00:28:54.833 --> 00:28:56.767
What is that supposed to mean?

00:28:56.835 --> 00:29:00.100
Keep your voice down.

00:29:01.840 --> 00:29:04.035
Once your girlfriend
talks to the Captain,

00:29:04.109 --> 00:29:05.542
they'll drag you
straight to Sick Bay.

00:29:05.610 --> 00:29:09.046
One neural scan,
and they'll know all about us.

00:29:09.114 --> 00:29:11.878
Well, maybe it's time they did.

00:29:11.950 --> 00:29:13.713
Think you can just walk away?

00:29:13.785 --> 00:29:14.877
Watch me.

00:29:14.953 --> 00:29:17.387
So, I guess this is
the real Tom Paris.

00:29:17.455 --> 00:29:19.047
Life throws up a few roadblocks,

00:29:19.124 --> 00:29:20.386
and he heads
for the nearest exit.

00:29:20.458 --> 00:29:22.187
Get away from me!

00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:23.522
I need you.

00:29:23.595 --> 00:29:24.687
You should've thought of that

00:29:24.763 --> 00:29:26.025
before you tried
to kill B'Elanna.

00:29:26.097 --> 00:29:27.564
Sick Bay.

00:29:27.632 --> 00:29:30.226
Remember how you felt
when you first saw me?

00:29:30.301 --> 00:29:32.064
You knew we were
meant to be together.

00:29:32.137 --> 00:29:34.230
- I was wrong.
- Think of how it feels

00:29:34.305 --> 00:29:35.431
when you're sitting at the helm

00:29:35.507 --> 00:29:37.907
- and the interface is active.
- It's over, Alice!

00:29:37.976 --> 00:29:40.672
One way or the other, I'm
getting the hell away from you.

00:29:40.745 --> 00:29:43.179
I'm sorry you feel that way.

00:29:46.484 --> 00:29:48.076
What are you doing to me?!

00:29:48.153 --> 00:29:50.246
Convincing you to
do the right thing.

00:29:50.321 --> 00:29:53.085
Take us to the Shuttle Bay.
We're leaving Voyager.

00:29:53.158 --> 00:29:54.591
No!

00:29:55.660 --> 00:29:56.752
Please, Tom.

00:29:56.828 --> 00:29:58.420
I don't want to hurt you.

00:29:58.496 --> 00:30:00.088
The Shuttle Bay, now.

00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:05.765
Deck 10. Shuttle Bay.

00:30:10.341 --> 00:30:12.935
This isn't the first time
you and Tom have had an argument

00:30:13.011 --> 00:30:14.774
about how he spends
his free time.

00:30:14.846 --> 00:30:16.609
This wasn't a lovers' quarrel.

00:30:16.681 --> 00:30:19.275
Captain, he practically
assaulted me.

00:30:19.350 --> 00:30:21.443
Well, that doesn't sound
like Tom.

00:30:21.519 --> 00:30:23.384
It wasn't Tom.
It was Alice.

00:30:23.454 --> 00:30:25.445
Now you've lost me.

00:30:25.523 --> 00:30:28.117
That's the name
that he's calling this new ship.

00:30:28.193 --> 00:30:30.787
Ever since he started working
on it, he hasn't slept.

00:30:30.862 --> 00:30:32.955
He's become irritable,
irrational...

00:30:33.031 --> 00:30:35.226
It's not just me;
Chakotay and Harry

00:30:35.300 --> 00:30:37.131
have noticed the same thing.

00:30:37.202 --> 00:30:41.696
This new ship... it has some kind
of neurogenic interface.

00:30:41.773 --> 00:30:45.300
Exactly. It must be having
some kind of an effect on him.

00:30:45.376 --> 00:30:48.311
All right, I'll have the Doctor
take a look at him,

00:30:48.379 --> 00:30:49.846
but in the meantime,
I want you...

00:30:49.914 --> 00:30:51.939
Captain, we have an unauthorized
launch in progress.

00:30:54.986 --> 00:30:57.477
Seal the Shuttle Bay doors.

00:30:57.555 --> 00:30:59.455
Too late. He's out.

00:31:03.528 --> 00:31:04.460
His shields are up.

00:31:04.529 --> 00:31:05.928
I can't get a transporter lock.

00:31:05.997 --> 00:31:07.396
Tractor beam.

00:31:07.465 --> 00:31:10.093
They're trying to tractor us.

00:31:10.168 --> 00:31:11.601
- Stop them.
- I can't.

00:31:11.669 --> 00:31:12.931
You'll be able
to maneuver much better

00:31:13.004 --> 00:31:15.768
if you complete the interface.

00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:17.102
How?

00:31:17.175 --> 00:31:20.144
Activate
the connector sequence.

00:31:28.419 --> 00:31:30.114
We're one now, Tom.

00:31:30.188 --> 00:31:34.784
Think of what you want me
to do, and I'll do it.

00:31:34.859 --> 00:31:39.125
We can disrupt
their tractor beam...

00:31:39.197 --> 00:31:40.960
with an optronic pulse.

00:31:41.032 --> 00:31:44.627
Good. You have access
to our weapons.

00:31:44.702 --> 00:31:46.169
Use them.

00:31:48.506 --> 00:31:50.599
He's charging weapons.

00:31:50.675 --> 00:31:52.973
Full power to the shields.

00:31:53.044 --> 00:31:54.978
He's disrupting
our tractor beam.

00:31:55.046 --> 00:31:56.308
Increase power to the emitters.

00:31:56.381 --> 00:31:58.781
We'll drag him in by his heels
if we have to.

00:31:59.884 --> 00:32:01.818
He's broken free, Captain.

00:32:01.886 --> 00:32:03.410
Janeway to Paris.

00:32:03.488 --> 00:32:06.116
Stand down and return
to Voyager immediately.

00:32:06.190 --> 00:32:08.021
I'm with Alice now, Captain.

00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:09.024
Let us go.

00:32:09.093 --> 00:32:10.890
You know I can't do that, Tom.

00:32:10.962 --> 00:32:12.759
She'll do anything
to get you back.

00:32:12.830 --> 00:32:15.264
I don't blame her for that,
but we have to stop her.

00:32:15.333 --> 00:32:16.595
How?

00:32:16.668 --> 00:32:19.364
You know.

00:32:19.437 --> 00:32:20.927
He's coming about.

00:32:21.072 --> 00:32:23.267
He's charging weapons again.

00:32:23.341 --> 00:32:24.501
Direct hit.

00:32:24.575 --> 00:32:26.304
Return fire.

00:32:26.377 --> 00:32:27.742
He's gone to warp.

00:32:27.812 --> 00:32:28.744
Track him.

00:32:28.813 --> 00:32:30.940
He masked his warp signature.

00:32:31.015 --> 00:32:32.141
He's gone.

00:32:42.360 --> 00:32:45.796
"And Daedalus fashioned wings
from wax and feathers

00:32:45.863 --> 00:32:48.798
and used them
to escape his prison."

00:32:48.866 --> 00:32:51.300
That's one of my favorite myths.

00:32:51.369 --> 00:32:53.303
I know.

00:32:53.371 --> 00:32:55.703
But you left out
the part where Icarus

00:32:55.773 --> 00:32:58.674
flew too close to the
sun and his wings melted.

00:33:00.078 --> 00:33:01.670
Poetic license.

00:33:01.746 --> 00:33:04.214
Besides, if we get
too close to a star,

00:33:04.282 --> 00:33:07.217
we have multiphasic
shielding to protect us.

00:33:09.253 --> 00:33:11.187
What is it?

00:33:11.255 --> 00:33:12.916
My arms.

00:33:13.024 --> 00:33:15.219
They feel numb.

00:33:15.293 --> 00:33:17.386
Who needs arms
when you have wings?

00:33:17.462 --> 00:33:19.555
You're becoming
a part of me now.

00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:21.723
Our potential is unlimited.

00:33:21.799 --> 00:33:25.792
Forget the old Tom Paris.
He doesn't exist anymore.

00:33:33.711 --> 00:33:35.542
You know my policy.

00:33:35.613 --> 00:33:37.808
We're not looking for a refund...
just some information.

00:33:37.882 --> 00:33:39.611
That's one commodity
I don't keep in stock.

00:33:39.684 --> 00:33:41.549
I suggest you look elsewhere.

00:33:41.619 --> 00:33:43.519
Not until we get some answers.

00:33:43.588 --> 00:33:47.456
You'll find I'm prepared to
deal with disgruntled customers.

00:33:47.525 --> 00:33:49.459
Captain, I'm reading
active weapons signatures

00:33:49.527 --> 00:33:51.290
on three of the derelict ships.

00:33:51.362 --> 00:33:52.954
They are targeting Voyager.

00:33:53.031 --> 00:33:55.465
Before we take actions
we both might regret,

00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:58.297
Mr. Neelix has
something to show you.

00:33:58.369 --> 00:34:05.400
I wanted to say, uh... thank you
for this... lost treasure.

00:34:05.476 --> 00:34:07.740
A beryllium crystal.

00:34:07.812 --> 00:34:10.576
I'm surprised
a trader of your distinction

00:34:10.648 --> 00:34:13.412
would let this slip
through this fingers.

00:34:13.484 --> 00:34:16.351
I could say
all trades are final,

00:34:16.421 --> 00:34:19.447
but we'd be willing
to give it back

00:34:19.524 --> 00:34:22.084
in exchange
for some cooperation.

00:34:24.495 --> 00:34:25.427
Haunted?

00:34:25.496 --> 00:34:27.088
That's what
the Haakonian told me

00:34:27.165 --> 00:34:28.257
when he traded her.

00:34:28.332 --> 00:34:31.096
I blamed his wild stories
on isolation sickness

00:34:31.169 --> 00:34:33.262
and then took
the ship off his hands.

00:34:33.337 --> 00:34:35.601
Did you ever notice
anything odd about the ship?

00:34:35.673 --> 00:34:37.402
Odd? You could say that.

00:34:37.475 --> 00:34:39.443
I tried turning her
into a towing vessel.

00:34:39.510 --> 00:34:40.602
She was cooperative at first,

00:34:40.678 --> 00:34:42.202
but then she began
to require constant...

00:34:43.281 --> 00:34:44.942
I hope you haven't forgotten me.

00:34:48.352 --> 00:34:49.910
Mr. Abaddon?

00:34:49.987 --> 00:34:52.455
Wh-where was I?

00:34:52.523 --> 00:34:53.581
Constant repairs.

00:34:53.658 --> 00:34:55.649
Right. Please...

00:34:55.726 --> 00:34:57.626
I wasn't going
to tell them anything.

00:34:57.695 --> 00:34:59.094
Who are you speaking to?

00:34:59.163 --> 00:35:01.461
No one. I-I-I have to leave now.

00:35:01.532 --> 00:35:03.295
I'll return the items
you traded for the ship.

00:35:03.367 --> 00:35:05.232
Leave me alone.

00:35:05.303 --> 00:35:07.237
I did what you told me.
I found you a pilot.

00:35:07.305 --> 00:35:08.499
What is it...
what are you seeing?

00:35:08.573 --> 00:35:09.505
It's her.

00:35:09.574 --> 00:35:10.734
She's right in front of me.

00:35:10.808 --> 00:35:11.900
There's no one there.

00:35:11.976 --> 00:35:13.409
Transport me back now.

00:35:18.316 --> 00:35:21.683
Janeway to Sick Bay.
Medical emergency.

00:35:21.752 --> 00:35:23.583
He suffered
a cerebral hemorrhage.

00:35:23.654 --> 00:35:25.918
Fortunately, I was able
to repair the damage in time.

00:35:25.990 --> 00:35:27.252
What caused it?

00:35:27.325 --> 00:35:29.759
It appears his neural pathways
were recently restructured.

00:35:29.827 --> 00:35:32.762
I detected
a neurogenic signature.

00:35:32.830 --> 00:35:35.424
Looks like Alice
got to him, too.

00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:37.491
Wake him.

00:35:41.005 --> 00:35:42.768
Oh. She was here.

00:35:42.840 --> 00:35:45.308
The woman you saw
was an hallucination

00:35:45.376 --> 00:35:47.936
created by the derelict ship's
neurogenic interface.

00:35:48.012 --> 00:35:49.946
I've given you
a cortical suppressant.

00:35:50.014 --> 00:35:51.948
She won't be
bothering you anymore.

00:35:52.016 --> 00:35:55.782
Tell me, what does this ship
want with our crewman?

00:35:55.853 --> 00:35:57.286
She can't fly herself.

00:35:57.355 --> 00:35:59.619
She needs a pilot...
a biological entity

00:35:59.690 --> 00:36:01.954
to work in tandem
with her programming.

00:36:02.026 --> 00:36:03.391
Well, if all she
needed was a pilot,

00:36:03.461 --> 00:36:05.361
why didn't she just recruit you?

00:36:07.298 --> 00:36:09.232
I wasn't compatible.

00:36:09.300 --> 00:36:12.565
She... said my reflexes
were too slow,

00:36:12.637 --> 00:36:16.403
that I was as useless
as the junk that I traded,

00:36:16.474 --> 00:36:19.568
that I couldn't get her
to where she needed to go.

00:36:19.644 --> 00:36:21.703
Don't ask me
for the coordinates.

00:36:21.779 --> 00:36:22.711
She never told me.

00:36:22.780 --> 00:36:26.409
Just insisted that I get her
a real pilot.

00:36:26.484 --> 00:36:30.921
I'm sorry I didn't
warn you before.

00:36:30.988 --> 00:36:33.218
I couldn't resist her.

00:36:33.291 --> 00:36:35.225
Seven of Nine
to Captain Janeway.

00:36:35.293 --> 00:36:37.955
Please report to Astrometrics.

00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:44.763
I've managed
to reconstruct the data

00:36:44.835 --> 00:36:46.427
Ensign Paris was working on.

00:36:46.504 --> 00:36:47.766
My suspicion was correct.

00:36:47.838 --> 00:36:48.770
It is a course trajectory.

00:36:48.839 --> 00:36:50.704
Let's see it.

00:36:50.775 --> 00:36:53.437
It terminates
in Spatial Grid 867.

00:36:53.511 --> 00:36:55.069
Looks uninhabited.

00:36:55.146 --> 00:36:59.082
It's empty space with the
exception of a small anomaly.

00:36:59.150 --> 00:37:02.085
A particle fountain.

00:37:02.153 --> 00:37:04.713
The Federation lost
more than a dozen ships

00:37:04.789 --> 00:37:08.054
examining a similar phenomenon
in the Alpha Quadrant.

00:37:08.125 --> 00:37:11.060
Relay the coordinates
to the Bridge.

00:37:11.128 --> 00:37:13.096
Take us out of warp.

00:37:15.466 --> 00:37:17.229
Can you see it now?

00:37:17.301 --> 00:37:19.735
Yes.

00:37:25.176 --> 00:37:27.269
What is it?

00:37:29.480 --> 00:37:31.778
Home.

00:37:40.992 --> 00:37:41.924
Distance?

00:37:41.993 --> 00:37:43.085
Six million kilometers.

00:37:43.160 --> 00:37:45.094
Decrease speed
to one-quarter impulse.

00:37:45.162 --> 00:37:46.254
Full power to shields.

00:37:46.330 --> 00:37:48.924
I'm detecting a vessel
off our starboard bow.

00:37:49.066 --> 00:37:50.260
It's Tom.

00:37:50.334 --> 00:37:51.926
He's headed
right for the anomaly.

00:37:52.003 --> 00:37:53.595
Can you get a transporter lock?

00:37:53.671 --> 00:37:54.695
No, ma'am,

00:37:54.772 --> 00:37:56.763
not with those multiphasic
shields in place.

00:37:56.841 --> 00:37:58.103
Are we in hailing range?

00:37:58.175 --> 00:37:59.870
Opening a channel.

00:37:59.944 --> 00:38:01.104
He's responding.

00:38:01.178 --> 00:38:04.079
Keep your distance, Captain,
or we'll open fire.

00:38:04.148 --> 00:38:05.206
Tom, listen to me.

00:38:05.283 --> 00:38:07.717
The neurogenic interface
is affecting your judgment.

00:38:07.785 --> 00:38:10.379
Drop your shields
and let us beam you aboard.

00:38:10.454 --> 00:38:12.422
Ignore them.
Keep going.

00:38:14.959 --> 00:38:16.324
He's not responding.

00:38:16.394 --> 00:38:18.419
Target his propulsion systems

00:38:18.496 --> 00:38:19.929
and fire.

00:38:22.199 --> 00:38:23.689
Direct hit.

00:38:23.768 --> 00:38:25.065
The vessel's shields
are holding.

00:38:25.136 --> 00:38:26.364
Doctor to the Bridge.

00:38:26.437 --> 00:38:27.563
Cease fire.

00:38:27.638 --> 00:38:29.401
Ensign Paris' neural readings
are fluctuating.

00:38:29.473 --> 00:38:32.408
His synaptic functions
have become linked to the ship.

00:38:32.476 --> 00:38:35.912
If we keep firing,
we could injure him severely.

00:38:35.980 --> 00:38:37.072
Acknowledged.

00:38:37.148 --> 00:38:38.080
Tuvok, stand down.

00:38:38.149 --> 00:38:39.741
We've got ten minutes
until he reaches

00:38:39.817 --> 00:38:40.909
the particle fountain.

00:38:40.985 --> 00:38:42.418
Is there any way
to disable their shields

00:38:42.486 --> 00:38:43.783
without firing weapons?

00:38:43.854 --> 00:38:45.913
If I could access
their main computer

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:47.719
and transmit
a shutdown sequence...

00:38:47.792 --> 00:38:49.760
Problem is,
Tom and Alice would detect it.

00:38:49.827 --> 00:38:51.590
They'd compensate.

00:38:51.662 --> 00:38:53.596
Unless we find a way
to distract them.

00:38:53.664 --> 00:38:54.926
Bridge to the Doctor.

00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:56.261
Go ahead.

00:38:56.334 --> 00:38:58.768
Any progress on your analysis
of the neurogenic interface?

00:38:58.836 --> 00:39:00.269
Not yet, Captain.

00:39:00.338 --> 00:39:01.430
Would it be possible to tap

00:39:01.505 --> 00:39:03.234
into the interface
using a com signal?

00:39:03.307 --> 00:39:05.036
I believe so,

00:39:05.109 --> 00:39:07.270
but I don't know
what that would accomplish.

00:39:07.345 --> 00:39:09.074
You've got five minutes; do it.

00:39:09.146 --> 00:39:11.546
And tell B'Elanna to prepare
for an away mission.

00:39:11.615 --> 00:39:14.083
Captain?

00:39:19.156 --> 00:39:20.214
We're four minutes away.

00:39:20.291 --> 00:39:21.280
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:39:21.359 --> 00:39:22.724
- Status?
- Stand by, Captain.

00:39:22.793 --> 00:39:24.556
I'm making
the final adjustments.

00:39:24.628 --> 00:39:27.563
I'm not sure how I feel
about getting inside Tom's head.

00:39:27.631 --> 00:39:29.394
Maybe you'll be able
to explain a few things

00:39:29.467 --> 00:39:31.196
when you get back.

00:39:31.268 --> 00:39:33.327
I knew you were the one.

00:39:33.404 --> 00:39:37.397
No one's ever gotten me
this close before.

00:39:37.475 --> 00:39:40.069
I'll have you home
in just a few minutes.

00:39:40.144 --> 00:39:43.580
I promise you won't
be disappointed.

00:39:43.647 --> 00:39:44.978
Don't believe her.

00:39:46.050 --> 00:39:47.915
Where's Alice?

00:39:48.052 --> 00:39:49.747
There is no Alice.

00:39:49.820 --> 00:39:52.311
She's a pile of circuits
in this ship's computer core.

00:39:52.390 --> 00:39:55.553
You're letting
a program delude you.

00:39:55.626 --> 00:39:58.925
Doctor to Bridge.
She's in.

00:39:59.063 --> 00:40:00.587
Now.

00:40:00.664 --> 00:40:03.189
Accessing their main computer.

00:40:03.267 --> 00:40:04.598
You don't understand.

00:40:04.668 --> 00:40:06.431
This is what I've
always dreamed of.

00:40:06.504 --> 00:40:08.938
You're still dreaming,
and when you wake up,

00:40:09.006 --> 00:40:10.098
you're in for a big surprise.

00:40:10.174 --> 00:40:11.106
Alice needs me.

00:40:11.175 --> 00:40:12.267
So do I.

00:40:12.343 --> 00:40:13.571
Nice sentiment, but it's a lie.

00:40:13.644 --> 00:40:16.112
Your family will do anything
to keep us apart.

00:40:16.180 --> 00:40:17.442
Don't listen to them.

00:40:17.515 --> 00:40:19.107
Tom, it's me, B'Elanna.

00:40:19.183 --> 00:40:20.946
Alice is an illusion.

00:40:21.018 --> 00:40:22.610
I'm giving you
what you always wanted...

00:40:22.686 --> 00:40:24.119
something they could never do.

00:40:24.188 --> 00:40:26.179
Does that sound
like an illusion?

00:40:26.257 --> 00:40:28.782
I can't... think.

00:40:28.859 --> 00:40:31.089
Leave me alone, both of you.

00:40:31.162 --> 00:40:33.460
They've accessed our systems.

00:40:33.531 --> 00:40:35.328
They're trying
to disable my shields.

00:40:35.399 --> 00:40:36.331
Stop them.

00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:39.426
Focus on me.
Listen to me.

00:40:39.503 --> 00:40:40.970
My shields are failing.
Do something!

00:40:41.105 --> 00:40:43.539
It's time to come home.

00:40:43.607 --> 00:40:44.574
Tom.

00:40:44.642 --> 00:40:45.574
No!

00:40:45.643 --> 00:40:48.237
Hang on. We're going
to get you out of here.

00:40:48.312 --> 00:40:49.210
Tom!

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:50.872
No!

00:40:52.450 --> 00:40:53.382
I've got it, Captain.

00:40:53.451 --> 00:40:54.383
Their shields are down.

00:40:54.452 --> 00:40:55.976
Beam him to Sick Bay.

00:40:56.053 --> 00:40:58.647
There's too much interference
from the particle fountain.

00:40:58.722 --> 00:41:00.656
I'm boosting
the confinement beam.

00:41:00.724 --> 00:41:02.248
Try it now.

00:41:02.326 --> 00:41:04.055
We've got him!

00:41:05.129 --> 00:41:08.292
Alice is losing helm control.

00:41:16.640 --> 00:41:19.302
Resume course
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:41:26.517 --> 00:41:28.781
You'll need a few days
to fully recover.

00:41:28.853 --> 00:41:29.945
Think you can manage

00:41:30.020 --> 00:41:31.612
to stay off your feet
for that long?

00:41:31.689 --> 00:41:33.623
If he doesn't,
I'll break his legs.

00:41:33.691 --> 00:41:37.991
Well, then, I'll leave you
to B'Elanna's tender mercies.

00:41:39.363 --> 00:41:42.628
I've got something for you.

00:41:42.700 --> 00:41:45.794
It's a get well card
from Naomi Wildman.

00:41:45.870 --> 00:41:47.132
It's a pretty good
likeness of you,

00:41:47.204 --> 00:41:51.163
but I don't think
she quite captured my eyes.

00:41:56.046 --> 00:41:58.981
I'm sorry...

00:41:59.049 --> 00:42:00.983
for everything.

00:42:01.051 --> 00:42:03.611
It wasn't your fault.

00:42:06.323 --> 00:42:09.759
But I remember all of it...

00:42:09.827 --> 00:42:14.287
everything I said,
everything I did...

00:42:15.666 --> 00:42:19.261
It was like I was sleepwalking.

00:42:19.336 --> 00:42:22.965
The important thing
is you woke up.

00:42:24.174 --> 00:42:26.301
Yeah.

00:42:28.012 --> 00:42:31.470
Thanks for being my alarm clock.

00:42:35.352 --> 00:42:38.150
Anytime.

00:42:39.223 --> 00:42:42.784
From now on...

00:42:42.860 --> 00:42:45.954
I promise no more affairs
with strange ships.

00:42:46.030 --> 00:42:48.965
What about the Delta Flyer?

00:42:52.202 --> 00:42:55.330
We're just friends.
